      "content": "In a high-fidelity actuarial model, you should prioritize granular data on objective behavioral factors like specific employment sectors, household formation rates, and utility consumption patterns rather than attempting to quantify cultural traits or group-specific risk profiles.\n\nYou can effectively capture these nuances by analyzing how the influx alters local supply chains and infrastructure stressors, which are direct drivers of loss severity without relying on protected demographic characteristics. This approach allows you to model the economic adaptedness of new communities while maintaining compliance and avoiding discriminatory biases in your pricing strategies.",
